\item Fit a CoE plus thick shell in both Newtonian gravity and relativistic LTB\cite{Lemaitre1933,Tolman1934,Bondi1947}.
\item Orient the model on the Galactic sky: untilted, then \(+15^\circ\) tilt, then a radial gradient, then an \(+80.8^\circ\) roll about the CoE axis, matching Migkas Fig.~8.
\item Evolve the donut-universe picture---shells expanding outward faster than light in a coordinate sense, while the sphere of events visible to us grows at \(c\), with recombination as a spherical surface of fixed physical radius around the CoE.
\item Stress-test the CMB: compute the gravitational multipole on the last-scattering sky, form the kill function (the electromagnetic temperature multipole opposite in sign to that gravitational multipole), and compare exploratory two-emitter and multipole-partner constructions.
\end{enumerate}
